export anchor RacingTelemetryStyle:
    number: 136
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Racing telemetry
    idea: A daylight timing screen where projects race in a position tower, progress reads as three sector bars, and italic slanted numbers carry the speed.
    base: light
    palette:
        pitLane: #f3f4f6, the page, nav tabs and field fill
        panel: #ffffff, panels and the header
        tarmac: #1c1f24, text, position chips, sector fill and checkers
        muted: #545a63, keys, gaps and axes
        line: #d5d8dd, row rules and grid
        raceRed: #c8102e, brand plate, primary button, this week line, Behind
        purple: #6a1fb0, best sectors, the best day and focus
        green: #1a7a35, On track and the Research team bar
        amber: #8c5a00, At risk text
        flagYellow: #f6c90e, the race control flag, never text
    type:
        Sans uses Helvetica Neue, Arial Black, Arial, mostly italic 800 to
        900 caps. Numbers use DIN Alternate, Bahnschrift, Roboto Condensed,
        Arial Narrow in italic. Mono for gaps and times uses SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas. Hero numbers 48px, greeting 40px caps, panel titles 18px
        caps, project names 16px italic, body 14px, keys 11px italic caps.
    layout:
        A checkered band runs across the top and again before the sheet.
        The header has a red slanted brand plate, an underlined search, a
        slanted red New project button, a round bell and Driver Mara
        Okafor, then slanted nav tabs with the current one black with a red
        base. The race row has the date, a big italic caps greeting and a
        Race control message bar with a yellow flag cell, beside four
        slanted number tiles with thick left bars. The Timing tower table
        orders projects by completion from P1 to P6 with a slanted position
        chip, a team colour bar, name and category, three sector bars,
        tasks, percent, gap in points to the leader, due and status. The
        right column holds a Pace line chart comparing this week solid red
        against last week dashed by weekday, and Team radio activity. The
        table scrolls inside its panel on small screens.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 10px table cells, 24px between panels.
    density: Dense in the tower, airy in the hero numbers.
    corners: None. Shapes are parallelograms slanted minus 12 degrees instead of rounded.
    borders: 1px light line on panels, a 3px tarmac rule under panel titles, 6px left bars on number tiles.
    shadows: None.
    icons: Filled circle for On track, half filled diamond for At risk, downward triangle for Behind, as position change marks beside the italic caps word.
    focus: A 3px purple outline offset 2px.
    tone: Pit wall shorthand in italic caps, such as Timing tower, Race control, Pace, Team radio, Leader and plus 18.
